{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.GCD","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.without_eps_eq_the_conclusion_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.without_eps_eq_the_conclusion_fails","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L144-L149","doc":"**The hypothesis is what carries the content, not the arithmetic.** With `eps` free\nof `u * v` the conclusion can fail — `Δ = 2` does not divide `3`. Recorded so\n`chain_mubar_vanishes` is visibly a statement about `eps_eq` rather than a triviality\nthat would hold for any coefficient whatsoever. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L140-L142","doc":"…and the divisibility genuinely fires on it: `2 ∣ 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain_eps_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain_eps_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L138-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain_delta_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain_delta_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L135-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.carrierChain","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L125-L133","doc":"**Not vacuous**: an instance with `Δ ≥ 2` and a genuinely nonzero coefficient,\nmatching the carrier's measured values (`lk = ±2` on consecutive components, all-`σ⁻¹`\nbranch). Recorded so `chain_mubar_vanishes` cannot be read as holding because the\ncoefficient is always zero — here it is `4`, and `Δ = 2` divides it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.both_orderings_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.both_orderings_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L114-L123","doc":"The reverse ordering `ε_{y,x}(λ_hub)` is measured to be `0` (596/596), and `Δ`\ndivides that too — trivially.\n\nStated because the raw coefficient is order-DEPENDENT (`u·v` one way, `0` the other),\nwhich is alarming until one notices that this is exactly what the mod-`Δ` indeterminacy\nabsorbs: the invariant is well defined and zero under **both** orderings, so nothing\nabout the vanishing depends on a convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.chain_mubar_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.chain_mubar_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L104-L112","doc":"**The result, and it is the whole file.** `μ̄` is defined modulo `Δ`, and `Δ` divides\nthe chain triple's coefficient — so `μ̄ = 0` there.\n\nThe proof is `gcd u v ∣ u ∣ u * v`. It is unconditional in `u` and `v`: no positivity,\nno primality, no bound on the linking numbers. All the content sits in `eps_eq`, which\nis where monotonicity was used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.delta","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L100-L102","doc":"Milnor's indeterminacy for a chain triple. The third linking number vanishes by the\nchain hypothesis, so `Δ = gcd(u, v, 0)` collapses to `gcd(u, v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.eps_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.eps_eq","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L98-L98","doc":"MEASURED (596/596 monotone): the far meridians are non-interleaved, so the\ncoefficient is the product of the two linking numbers ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.eps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.eps","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L95-L95","doc":"the degree-2 Magnus coefficient `ε_{x,y}(λ_hub)` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.v","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.v","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L93-L93","doc":"`lk(hub, y)` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.u","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L91-L91","doc":"`lk(hub, x)` — nonzero by the chain hypothesis, though nothing below needs that ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple","kind":"structure","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.lean#L81-L98","doc":"A **chain triple** on a monotone closure: a hub linked to two ends `x, y` that are\nunlinked from each other, together with the degree-2 Magnus coefficient of the hub's\nlongitude.\n\n`eps_eq` is the measured structural input and the only place monotonicity enters: one\nrun per generator puts the two far meridians in contiguous, non-interleaved blocks of\n`λ_hub`, so the coefficient is a product of block sums. Verified on 596/596 monotone\nchain triples; it fails off monotone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}